WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.430
A shop keeps a complaints counter.

2
00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:08.400
Week by week it ticks over:
two, four, three, one, three.

3
00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:10.620
About three a week, on average.

4
00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:12.140
Nothing unusual.

5
00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:15.110
Then one week, the counter jumps to eight.

6
00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:16.610
Is that just bad luck?

7
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.070
Or is something really going wrong?

8
00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:22.980
In this mission, you'll model random
events that happen independently,

9
00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:26.950
at a uniform average rate,
with the Poisson distribution.

10
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.940
You'll ask: if nothing has changed, how
likely is a result at least as extreme

11
00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:33.390
as the one you saw?

12
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:36.650
And you'll compare that p-value
with a significance level:

13
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:39.810
below it, you reject the null hypothesis.

14
00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:45.010
Your mission: decide whether eight
complaints means bad luck or a real problem.
